==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Stall the first Lemurr for cash while you prepare for Cadaver Bear. You have time for around 2 Worker Cat levels before you need to start saving up or spawning units to deal with the LeMurr, who is not much of a problem until Cadaver Bear joins him a bit later.

Fight Cadaver Bear like always, long ranged/rusher units with proper meatshielding from [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]]. Watch out for his burrow, and hit him with a [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] to knock him out of the animation; be prepared to deal with him and LeMurr at the same time as Lemurr continues to spawn through out the match. Being prepared for Cadaver Bear is the biggest hurdle here, so chip him with units such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]] and be ready to Holy Blast when it looks like he's about to die (after his 3rd knockback), otherwise him reviving will pose an immense challenge.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The stage is nearly identical to Chapter 1, but with the enemies at a higher strength magnification and an additional Mistress Celeboodle for money. The Cadaver Bear will push hard, so try killing him as quickly as possible with the same strategy as Chapter 1: Holy Blasting him out of the ground and chipping him with [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]]. If you have unlocked [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] by this point, they will be an immensely useful asset for sneaking in hits on unburrowing Zombies, or even Cadaver Bear itself. You can use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to expedite the Cadaver Bear killing process if timed very well (not recommended if you trust your timing skills), but do be wary so as to not let Bahamut get the final hit.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage is almost identical to the regular Chapter 3 albeit with higher strength magnifications and replacement Zombie peons. The main threats here are 7 LeMurrs each with outstanding stats. Thankfully, they are Single Attack enemies, so rushing with mass meatshields and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is the optimal solution when dealing with them in order to prevent them from stacking.

